# Local Network File Sharing - code ownership (one owner per module)
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE:
# 1. Replace each placeholder handle (e.g. `@owner-discovery`) with the real GitHub username of that module's owner.
# 2. Once saved on `main`, GitHub AUTOMATICALLY:
#    - requests the owner's review on every PR that touches their module;
#    - requires the listed owners' sign-off for any change to /modules/contracts/.
#
# IMPORTANT: a change in /modules/contracts affects EVERY module. It needs review from the lead and the owners of
# the modules that use the changed type (see CONTRIBUTING.md, "The Contracts Stability Rule").
# Placeholders below follow the default 6-person split of the implementation plan.

# Shared contracts (M1) - lead + all consumers
/modules/contracts/          @aroosahoda @owner-discovery @owner-network @owner-transfer @owner-concurrency

# Device discovery (M2)
/modules/discovery/          @owner-discovery

# TCP networking & protocol (M3)
/modules/network/            @owner-network

# File services & integrity (M5) and transfer engine (M4)
/modules/file/               @owner-transfer
/modules/transfer/           @owner-transfer

# Concurrency & reliability (M6)
/modules/concurrency/        @owner-concurrency

# User interfaces (M7)
/modules/ui-cli/             @owner-ui
/modules/ui-javafx/          @owner-ui

